      "writtenOn": "2023-11-17T18:39:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah I\u0027m not worried about this specific use case, but trying to figure out how `prepareForReturnToCache` should behave in general. Like they way the comment reads for the function and how the cache behaves, a non-shareable resource will return to the cache when UsageRefs drop to zero. It really has nothing to do with CB refs. However, we\u0027re imposing a requirement on CB refs in this check because in this specific case of async maps we technically need that to be true.\n\nSo I was wondering if it makes sense to remove all checks on CB refs here. Then have a way to enforce that mappable dawn buffers (or all mappable buffers) can never add a CB ref.\n\nIn that model I\u0027m not too worried about multiple threads getting here since only one thread can be the last UsageRef.",
